1a. What is duck typing?
Duck typing means that an object can be used based on the methods or behavior it provides, rather than requiring it to belong to a particular class. Objects from unrelated classes can work with the same code as long as they provide the methods that code calls.

1b. What did the Car class need to have?
The Car class needed to provide the same methods called by the loop on the Dog and Cat objects. It did not need to inherit from Animal; it only needed to support the operations the loop expected.

